CompressedTensorsWNA8Int (int weights, int8 per-token activations) chose its kernel with choose_mp_linear_kernel and
act_type set to the params dtype, so on CUDA below SM90 the list reached Marlin before Humming. Marlin accepts the
layer and never reads _humming_input_quant_config, so a checkpoint that declares int8 activations served W4A16 on
a 3090 or a 4090, with nothing in the log beyond the kernel name. With an input quant the scheme now takes
HummingLinearKernel, the one mixed-precision kernel that reads it, and raises with Humming's reason when Humming
cannot implement the layer. Without one, the choice is vLLM's as before.

Kind: fix
What: compressed-tensors' W4A8 int scheme (CompressedTensorsWNA8Int) takes the Humming kernel when it has an
  input quant, where vLLM's kernel chooser took Marlin below SM90 and Marlin ignores the int8 input config
  (served W4A16, silently)
Upstream: none yet
Cut-against: 0.34.0
Retires-when: upstream fixes the kernel choice

